---
// The styles for the Keep DOM, as a component so every keep-fed page can carry them.
//
// They lived in keep.astro's own <style is:global> while that page was the only place a keep was drawn.
// The builders moved to src/lib/keep-view.js so more than one page can render a keep, and a plain .js
// module cannot carry an Astro style block — so the styles became a component, and each consuming page
// includes this once. Keep the block is:global and keep every selector prefixed keep-; both are
// asserted in tests/test_keep.py, because no gate can see a zero-area div.
---
<style is:global>
  /* Sized to be read from across a room: this is the one surface here meant for a television driven by a
     computer, not for a phone held at arm's length.

     is:global is load-bearing, not laziness. Astro scopes a plain <style> by stamping every element in the
     template with a data-astro-cid attribute — but everything the Keep pages draw below their mount
     point is built by document.createElement in src/lib/keep-view.js, so it never carries the attribute
     and no scoped rule can match it. Left scoped, the wheel renders 876x0 and every size below falls back
     to the browser's. Nothing here can collide: every selector is prefixed keep-. Same problem the
     profile-name dialog has, which faces.css solves the same way for the same reason. */
  .keep-day { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .keep-day h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .keep-focus { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0.15rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .keep-meals { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .keep-meal { min-width: 12rem; }
  .keep-meal-name { display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .keep-meal-dish { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .keep-appointments { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .keep-blocks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .keep-block { font-size: 1rem; }
  .keep-wheel-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  .keep-wheel { width: 15rem; height: 15rem; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; }
  .keep-key { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .keep-key li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.1rem; padding: 0.15rem 0; }
  .keep-swatch { width: 0.9rem; height: 0.9rem; border-radius: 50%; flex: none; }
  /* The Overview's fortnight grid and the day page's previous/next row: script-built like everything else
     here, so global for the same reason. Grid cells reuse .panel for their box; what is here is only what
     a panel does not already say. */
  .keep-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(11rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .keep-grid-cell { display: block; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .keep-grid-day { display: block; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .keep-grid-focus { display: block; font-size: 0.9rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .keep-grid-meals { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .keep-day-nav { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  /* Fork Knife's two menu views (src/lib/keep-view.js renderMenuByDish / renderMenuByDay). Script-built
     like the rest, so global for the same reason, and keep- prefixed like the rest because that is what
     makes global safe here. Both views are read at the same distance as the day panels above. */
  .keep-menu-slot { margin: 1rem 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .keep-menu-dishes { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .keep-menu-dish { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.25rem 0.75rem; padding: 0.3rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .keep-menu-name { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .keep-menu-dish .keep-menu-name { font-weight: 700; }
  .keep-menu-when { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  /* The household's own sentence about why extra is cooked: its own line, so it never competes with the
     dish name for the eye. flex-basis 100% is what breaks the row without a wrapper element. */
  .keep-menu-note { flex-basis: 100%; font-size: 0.95rem; font-style: italic; }
  .keep-menu-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; }
  .keep-menu-day h3 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .keep-menu-meals { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .keep-menu-meal { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: baseline; padding: 0.15rem 0; font-size: 1rem; }
  .keep-menu-meal .keep-menu-name { font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  /* Leftovers read quieter than a cook day: the dish is the same, the work is not. */
  .keep-menu-again { opacity: 0.8; }
</style>
